-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024 -- THE SEAT LAYER (neutral part).
--
-- SEAT: a person in Singapore who owns a television or a satellite dish, or who provides a broadcasting service, or who deals in a decoder, asking
-- "Do I need a licence?", "May I do this?", "Am I committing an offence?" and "What is the most I can be punished with or made to pay?".
-- Never the Authority's seat, the Minister's or a court's.
--
-- This file asks the questions that are about services, class licences, exemption orders and decoders (Parts 4 and 11). The questions about broadcasting APPARATUS
-- (a dish, a receiver: ss 20 and 47, the First Schedule, the TVRO System Regulations, composition under s 57) are in the quarantined file sgba-tv-seat.l4, because
-- what they answer is what NOTES.md may not state.
-- It IMPORTs the layer-1 modules and calls their rules; it restates none of them and no layer-1 module was changed for it. Every question has @export and an @desc on
-- each input, takes plain inputs a person could state (yes/no, a date, a number, a choice written out in words), and answers in a sentence.
-- Where the Act does not say, or the deposited text does not cover the date, the answer is the sentence "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date." -- the explicit not-covered value, never a guess.
--
-- Dates. Every dated question takes the day as an ISO date. The deposited text of the Act is the text in force from 25 September 2024 to 4 November 2026;
-- on any other day the answer is the not-covered sentence. (No past text of the Act or any instrument was obtained.)

§ `Helpers for wording answers`

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the answer to a yes or no question` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
    WHEN JUST b THEN IF b THEN "Yes." ELSE "No."

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the plain yes or no` MEANS IF b THEN "Yes." ELSE "No."

-- A service the person names in words, from the twenty items of the Second Schedule; any other wording is a service not on the list.
GIVEN `the service` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
`the Second Schedule item the words name` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the service` EQUALS "free-to-air nationwide television" THEN JUST `free-to-air nationwide television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "free-to-air localised television" THEN JUST `free-to-air localised television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "free-to-air international television" THEN JUST `free-to-air international television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription nationwide television" THEN JUST `subscription nationwide television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription localised television" THEN JUST `subscription localised television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription international television" THEN JUST `subscription international television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "special interest television" THEN JUST `special interest television services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "free-to-air nationwide radio" THEN JUST `free-to-air nationwide radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "free-to-air localised radio" THEN JUST `free-to-air localised radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "free-to-air international radio" THEN JUST `free-to-air international radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription nationwide radio" THEN JUST `subscription nationwide radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription localised radio" THEN JUST `subscription localised radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "subscription international radio" THEN JUST `subscription international radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "special interest radio" THEN JUST `special interest radio services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "audiotext" THEN JUST `audiotext services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "videotext" THEN JUST `videotext services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "teletext" THEN JUST `teletext services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "video-on-demand" THEN JUST `video-on-demand services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "broadcast data" THEN JUST `broadcast data services`
           IF ^ EQUALS "computer online" THEN JUST `computer online services`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- An act with a decoder, named in words from the nine acts of s 48(1).
GIVEN `the act` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Act with a decoder`
`the s 48(1) act the words name` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the act` EQUALS "manufacture" THEN JUST `manufacture`
           IF ^ EQUALS "assemble" THEN JUST `assemble`
           IF ^ EQUALS "modify" THEN JUST `modify`
           IF ^ EQUALS "import" THEN JUST `import`
           IF ^ EQUALS "export" THEN JUST `export`
           IF ^ EQUALS "sell" THEN JUST `sell`
           IF ^ EQUALS "offer for sale" THEN JUST `offer for sale`
           IF ^ EQUALS "let for hire" THEN JUST `let for hire`
           IF ^ EQUALS "otherwise distribute" THEN JUST `otherwise distribute`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN i IS A `Imprisonment`
GIVETH A STRING
`the imprisonment in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `no imprisonment is provided` THEN ", and no imprisonment"
    WHEN `imprisonment not exceeding` mo THEN CONCAT ", or imprisonment of up to ", TOSTRING mo, " months, or both"

GIVEN f IS A `Daily fine`
GIVETH A STRING
`the daily fine in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `no further daily fine is provided` THEN ""
    WHEN `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` amt THEN CONCAT ", and for a continuing offence a further fine of up to $", TOSTRING amt, " for every day or part of a day it continues after conviction"

GIVEN p IS A Punishment
GIVETH A STRING
`the punishment in words` MEANS
    CONCAT "A fine of up to $", TOSTRING (p's `fine not exceeding`), `the imprisonment in words` (p's `imprisonment`), `the daily fine in words` (p's `daily fine`), "."

§ `1. Providing a broadcasting service: do I need a licence?`

@export Do I need a broadcasting licence to provide this service in or from Singapore, and am I committing an offence if I provide it without one? Answers for a date inside the deposited text of the Act (25 September 2024 to 4 November 2026).
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `the service you provide` IS A STRING @desc The service, in words, as the Second Schedule lists it, for example "subscription nationwide television", "teletext", "audiotext", "computer online" or "video-on-demand"; any other wording is treated as a service not on the list.
      `it is or has ever been an online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service is, or has ever been, an online communication service within the Fourth Schedule (a social media service or an app distribution service).
      `you provide it in or from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service in or from Singapore.
      `you hold a broadcasting licence from the Authority under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Info-communications Media Development Authority has granted you a broadcasting licence under section 8 of the Act.
      `a class licence applies to your service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a class licence determined under section 9 applies to your service (for example, under the Class Licence Notification, or the digital display panels notification).
GIVETH A STRING
`Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` MEANS
    `the answer to a yes or no question` (`s 8(1) the person provides a licensable broadcasting service without the licence the subsection requires, on` `the day you ask about` (`the Second Schedule item the words name` `the service you provide`) `it is or has ever been an online communication service` `you provide it in or from Singapore` `you hold a broadcasting licence from the Authority under section 8` `a class licence applies to your service`)

@export If I provide a licensable broadcasting service without a licence and am convicted, what is the most I can be punished with?
GIVETH A STRING
`What is the most I can be punished with for providing a licensable broadcasting service without a licence?` MEANS
    `the punishment in words` `s 46 the punishment on conviction`

@export Is my service subject to a class licence under the Class Licence Notification (audiotext, videotext, teletext, broadcast data, VAN computer on-line, or an Internet content or service provider's computer on-line service)?
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `the service you provide` IS A STRING @desc The service, in words, for example "audiotext", "videotext", "teletext", "broadcast data" or "computer online".
      `it is a VAN computer on-line service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a computer on-line service licensed as a Value Added Network service under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act.
      `it is a computer on-line service provided by an Internet Content Provider or an Internet Service Provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide it as an Internet Content Provider or an Internet Service Provider as the Notification defines them.
      `the Authority has given you a notice under paragraph 3A(1) and the date in it has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority gave you a paragraph 3A(1) notice specifying a date, and that date has been reached.
GIVETH A STRING
`Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` MEANS
    `the answer to a yes or no question` (`N 1 para 3 the provision of the service is subject to the class licence, on` `the day you ask about` (`the Second Schedule item the words name` `the service you provide`) `it is a VAN computer on-line service` `it is a computer on-line service provided by an Internet Content Provider or an Internet Service Provider` `the Authority has given you a notice under paragraph 3A(1) and the date in it has been reached`)

@export Am I exempt from sections 8 and 9 because of the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order (news wire, financial information, weather or traffic, CCTV surveillance, in-flight, other computer on-line, or a service regulated by the Government)?
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `it is a news wire service transmitted primarily for news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is a news wire service where the information is transmitted primarily for news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies.
      `it is a financial information service transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is a financial information service where the information is transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition to its form.
      `it is a weather or traffic news service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is a weather or traffic news service.
      `it is a CCTV surveillance service for a single building or structure, solely for security surveillance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is a close circuit television surveillance service for reception within a single building or structure, provided solely for security surveillance.
      `it is an airline in-flight entertainment and information service on aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is an airline in-flight entertainment and information service provided on aircraft.
      `it is a computer on-line service that is not subject to a class licence or a paragraph 3A(1) notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is a computer on-line service that is not subject to a class licence under the Class Licence Notification or to a paragraph 3A(1) notice.
      `it is another licensable service regulated or licensed by the Government or a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is another licensable broadcasting service regulated or licensed by the Government, or a statutory authority, under a written law.
GIVETH A STRING
`Does the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order exempt me from sections 8 and 9?` MEANS
    `the answer to a yes or no question` (`O 1 para 1 the person who provides the service is exempt from sections 8 and 9 of the Act, on` `the day you ask about` `it is a news wire service transmitted primarily for news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies` `it is a financial information service transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition` `it is a weather or traffic news service` `it is a CCTV surveillance service for a single building or structure, solely for security surveillance` `it is an airline in-flight entertainment and information service on aircraft` `it is a computer on-line service that is not subject to a class licence or a paragraph 3A(1) notice` `it is another licensable service regulated or licensed by the Government or a statutory authority`)

@export Am I subject to the class licence for broadcasting to digital display panels (screens in public places or public transport)?
GIVEN `the day you ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2025-03-15.
      `you provide, in the course of business, a licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore for display on digital display panels` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide, in the course of business, a licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore comprising transmission of a programme for reception by and for display on digital display panels.
      `the number of those panels each in a public place in Singapore` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the panels are each in a public place in Singapore.
      `the number of those panels each installed in a public passenger transport vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the panels are each installed within a public passenger transport vehicle.
      `you are exempt by or under section 60 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are exempt by or under section 60 of the Act.
      `the panels are under the control of someone with a Films Act licence, a video games class licence or exemption, or a public entertainment licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the service solely for panels under the control or management of a person who holds a Films Act licence, is subject to the video games distribution class licence or its exemption, or holds a public entertainment licence (or is exempt from that Act).
GIVETH A STRING
`Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` MEANS
    `the answer to a yes or no question` (`S 477/2020 para 3(1) the person is subject to a class licence in connection with the service, on` `the day you ask about` `you provide, in the course of business, a licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore for display on digital display panels` `the number of those panels each in a public place in Singapore` `the number of those panels each installed in a public passenger transport vehicle` `you are exempt by or under section 60 of the Act` `the panels are under the control of someone with a Films Act licence, a video games class licence or exemption, or a public entertainment licence`)

§ `2. Decoders and encrypted programmes (section 48)`

@export May I manufacture, assemble, modify, import, export, sell, offer for sale, let for hire or distribute this decoder, or is that prohibited by section 48(1)?
GIVEN `what you do with the decoder` IS A STRING @desc One of: "manufacture", "assemble", "modify", "import", "export", "sell", "offer for sale", "let for hire", "otherwise distribute". Any other wording is not one of the acts section 48(1) lists.
      `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decoder is designed or adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be viewed in decoded form without the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service.
      `you know it is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know the decoder is an unauthorised decoder.
GIVETH A STRING
`Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 48(1) act the words name` `what you do with the decoder`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "The Act, as deposited, does not list that act in section 48(1)."
    WHEN JUST a THEN `the plain yes or no` (`s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited` a `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` `you know it is an unauthorised decoder`)

@export If it is proved that I did one of the acts in section 48(1) with an unauthorised decoder, will the court presume I knew it was unauthorised?
GIVEN `it is proved that you did the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is proved that you manufactured, assembled, modified, imported, exported, sold, offered for sale, let for hire or otherwise distributed an unauthorised decoder.
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence that you did not know the decoder was unauthorised.
GIVETH A STRING
`Does section 48(4) presume that I knew the decoder was unauthorised?` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 48(4) it is presumed that the person knew that the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` `it is proved that you did the act` `there is evidence to the contrary`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "Section 48(4) does not presume it on those facts."
    WHEN JUST b THEN `the plain yes or no` b

@export Is it an offence under section 48(2) to receive or rebroadcast this encrypted programme?
GIVEN `you wilfully receive or rebroadcast the encrypted programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you wilfully receive or rebroadcast an encrypted programme.
      `the programme has been decoded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the encrypted programme has been decoded.
      `the decoding was authorised by the lawful provider of the broadcasting service that broadcast it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decoding was done with the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service that broadcast the programme.
GIVETH A STRING
`Is my reception or rebroadcast of this programme prohibited by section 48(2)?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 48(2) the person's reception or rebroadcast is prohibited` `you wilfully receive or rebroadcast the encrypted programme` `the programme has been decoded` `the decoding was authorised by the lawful provider of the broadcasting service that broadcast it`)

@export If I am convicted of an offence under section 48, what is the most I can be punished with?
GIVETH A STRING
`What is the most I can be punished with for an offence under section 48?` MEANS
    `the punishment in words` `s 48(3) the punishment on conviction`

@export Can the broadcaster or the copyright owner sue me over an unauthorised decoder or decoded programme, and is it too late?
GIVEN `you did an act mentioned in section 48(1) with an unauthorised decoder that was used to decode an encrypted programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did one of the acts of section 48(1) with an unauthorised decoder, and the decoder was used to decode an encrypted programme.
      `the provider or the copyright owner has thereby suffered loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lawful provider of the broadcasting service or the owner of the copyright in the programme suffered loss or damage as a result.
      `the day of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc The day of the month on which you did the act, for example 10.
      `the month of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc The month in which you did the act, 1 to 12.
      `the year of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc The year in which you did the act, for example 2020.
      `the day the action is brought` IS A DATE @desc The day the civil action is or would be brought, in ISO 8601 form, for example 2026-03-10.
GIVETH A STRING
`May the provider or the copyright owner bring a civil action against me, and is it in time?` MEANS
    IF `s 48A(1) the lawful provider or the copyright owner may bring a civil action against the person` `you did an act mentioned in section 48(1) with an unauthorised decoder that was used to decode an encrypted programme` TRUE `the provider or the copyright owner has thereby suffered loss or damage`
    THEN (IF `s 48A(3) the action is not barred` `the day of the act` `the month of the act` `the year of the act` `the day the action is brought` THEN "Yes, and the action is within six years of the act." ELSE "Yes, but section 48A(3) bars an action brought after six years from the act.")
    ELSE "No: section 48A(1) needs the act, the decoding and the loss or damage."

§ `3. If something happens to me: investigation, officers, companies`

@export If I am an officer of a body corporate, or a partner, that commits an offence under the Act, can I be guilty as well?
GIVEN `the offence was committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was committed by a body corporate.
      `it is proved that it was committed with your consent or connivance, or attributable to your neglect, as an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is proved that the offence was committed with your consent or connivance, or is attributable to any neglect on your part, as an officer of the body corporate.
GIVETH A STRING
`Am I, as an officer, guilty as well as the body corporate?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 56(1) the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty of the offence` `the offence was committed by a body corporate` `it is proved that it was committed with your consent or connivance, or attributable to your neglect, as an officer`)

@export Is the court I am brought before one that can try an offence under the Broadcasting Act and impose the full penalty?
GIVEN `the court is a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is a District Court or a Magistrate's Court.
GIVETH A STRING
`Can this court try the offence and impose the full penalty?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 58 the court has jurisdiction to try an offence under this Act and power to impose the full penalty or punishment` `the court is a District Court or a Magistrate's Court`)

@export Does being punished under the Broadcasting Act stop me being prosecuted under another written law for the same act, or the other way round?
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under another written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the same act or omission is also an offence under another written law.
      `you have already been punished for that same offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been punished for that same offence.
GIVETH A STRING
`May I also be prosecuted under the other law, and punished by a higher or other penalty?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 54 the person may be prosecuted under the other written law and be liable to its punishment or penalty, higher or other than this Act's` `the act or omission is an offence under another written law` `you have already been punished for that same offence`)

@export If an officer asks me for documents or information under section 50, must I give them, and what can happen if I do not or lie?
GIVEN `the Authority or a person it authorised has by notice required the document or information within the period specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority, or a person it authorised, required the document or information by notice within a period the notice specifies.
      `it is within your knowledge, custody or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document or information is within your knowledge, custody or control.
GIVETH A STRING
`Must I provide the document or information the notice asks for?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 50(1) the person must provide the document or information` `the Authority or a person it authorised has by notice required the document or information within the period specified` `it is within your knowledge, custody or control`)

@export If I fail to comply with a section 50 notice, or alter, suppress or destroy a document, or give false information, what is the most I can be punished with?
GIVETH A STRING
`What is the most I can be punished with for failing to comply with a section 50 notice or for false information?` MEANS
    `the punishment in words` `s 50(4) the punishment on conviction of an offence under subsection (2) or (3)`

@export If I obstruct or hinder an employee or agent of the Authority, what is the most I can be punished with?
GIVETH A STRING
`What is the most I can be fined for obstructing or hindering an employee or agent of the Authority?` MEANS
    `the punishment in words` `s 49 the punishment on conviction`

§ `4. When a decision of the Authority goes against me`

@export If the Authority cancels or suspends my licence or fines me under section 12, how long do I have to appeal to the Minister?
GIVEN `the days since you received the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days since you received the Authority's written notice.
GIVETH A STRING
`Can I still appeal to the Minister against the Authority's decision under section 12?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 12(2) the aggrieved person may still appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` `the days since you received the notice`)

@export If the Authority proposes to modify the conditions of my broadcasting licence, how much time must I be given to make representations?
GIVEN `the days from service of the notice to the end of the time for representations` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the day the notice was served on you to the end of the time the notice gives for written representations.
GIVETH A STRING
`Is the time the notice gives me for representations long enough under section 10(2)?` MEANS
    `the plain yes or no` (`s 10(2) the notice is a notice the Authority must give before modifying` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the days from service of the notice to the end of the time for representations`)
